                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b232df6-3328-4fe2-9544-6e65e2727281",
                                                "sense_id": "d28cd203-0403-3f30-9d4e-ef132ccbabac",
                                                "text": "The factory increased its output this year."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e075a4a8-898c-4fad-9022-364d7da373e5",
                                                "sense_id": "d28cd203-0403-3f30-9d4e-ef132ccbabac",
                                                "text": "Output at the Pen-ch'i mine, which produced somewhat under 1 million tons annually during 1942-1944, was around 500,000 tons in 1949."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "225612c3-f35e-4dcd-a8ff-7ad917cc5fee",
                                                "sense_id": "d28cd203-0403-3f30-9d4e-ef132ccbabac",
                                                "text": "It misdesigned goods, adversely selected technologies, misallocated and misremunerated factors of production, encouraged work to rule, underproduced, misdistributed outputs and was subject to a myriad of moral hazards."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f1c0914-6930-43c1-ba75-11e2bd245327",
                                                "sense_id": "d28cd203-0403-3f30-9d4e-ef132ccbabac",
                                                "text": "Economics is a messy discipline: too fluid and unique to be a science, too rigorous to be an art. Perhaps it is fitting that economists’ most-used metric, gross domestic product (GDP), is a tangle too. GDP measures the total value of output in an economic territory. Its apparent simplicity explains why it is scrutinised down to tenths of a percentage point every month."
                                            }
                                        ]
